=== DEFECT FOUND AND FIXED ===

MY OWN FIRST DESIGN MADE ARCHIVAL IMPOSSIBLE.
The initial assess() treated "the object is itself in the ACTIVE set" as
protection (REASON_IS_ACTIVE_ROOT). Because IOM 2.1 permits ARCHIVED only from
ACTIVE, protecting every ACTIVE object protects everything: 31 of 39 round-1
probes failed, and no object could ever be archived. N-12 protects what
SUPPORTS current knowledge -- objects reachable from ANOTHER ACTIVE object --
not the candidate's own status, which is the precondition for archiving.
Fixed by _supports_other_active(), which excludes the candidate from the scan.
Bound by test_the_candidates_own_active_status_does_not_protect_it.

PRE-EXISTING GAP CLOSED (the task's purpose).
store.transition() permitted archiving any object, including one an ACTIVE
object derives from -- the hole recorded in the P1 technical debt as
"reachability guard has no mechanism". Now guarded at the sole mutation point.

TWO EXISTING TESTS CORRECTED, NOT WEAKENED.
test_archived_does_not_cascade and test_pti1_detects_membership_falling_below_two
both archived an object that ACTIVE knowledge still derived from -- legal only
because of the defect. Each was rewritten to reach the same state by a ratified
route (withdraw the dependent first / use RETRACTED), leaving both subjects --
what cascades, and PT-I1 membership -- unchanged.

=== SPECIFICATION NOTES ===
One apparent conflict, resolved by extraction rather than judgement. IOM 2.1
marks the ARCHIVED authority "Undefined (MISSING-31)", which would make this
task unimplementable. marker-crosswalk.md line 45 maps IOM MISSING-31 to
canonical M-38 ("Retention policy") and warns that canonical M-31 is a
different gap. M-38 is CLOSED by N-12, which supplies both trigger and owner.
Canonical M-31 (gate ownership) remains OPEN and is untouched.

A second, resolved the same way: N-12's Known Tension says REJECTED objects are
"subject to tiering like any other unreachable object", while R-2/IOM forbid
transitioning a terminal state. Compatible once CONTENT tiering is distinguished
from the ARCHIVED status transition. Only the ratified transition is implemented.

UNSPECIFIED AND DELIBERATELY NOT INVENTED:
  - The physical content-tiering step. N-12 says content becomes "retrievable
    through a slower path" but defines no tier, eviction or retrieval path.
    NO CONTENT IS EVICTED; reported by content_tiering_specified = False.
  - When tiering runs. "A maintenance operation" with no schedule or owner.
    Caller-invoked only; no scheduler, no GC, no age heuristic (N-12 rejected
    Option B), no hard deletion (I4, N-12 rejected Option E).
  - Retention of failure records and configuration: N-12 excludes them.
